adata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": false, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 16, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "8b75e6b5-5a8e-4366-9916-7c451817df6e", "reasoning_end_time": 1790284835.349402, "reasoning_recap_type": "collapse", "reasoning_start_time": 1790284818.9670675, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "e2debdd8-6527-40ab-bc54-8fde8b7fe23c", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "2f17f95c-4864-4fd5-81db-c6db12882f45", "working_turn_id": "2f17f95c-4864-4fd5-81db-c6db12882f45"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790284835.370158, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yeah — **this is the Yahoo team export, not Sleeper**, so I’m keeping the leagues separated. And looking at this roster, I get why you like it. The core is legit: Stafford, Cook, CeeDee, Davante, Ladd, Higgins, plus Andrews/Hockenson gives you plenty of weekly ceiling and trade flexibility. fileciteturn0file0L8-L20\n\nThe Higgins pick may have been earlier than you wanted, but it isn’t some roster-killing mistake. He’s sitting on your bench right now with a 92% Yahoo start rate / 99% roster rate, so he’s still a real asset rather than dead draft capital. fileciteturn0file0L17-L17 I’m much more interested in optimizing the fringes than trying to “correct” Higgins.\n\n### Defense: Carolina is actually fine **this week**\n\nYou currently have **Carolina @ Cleveland**. fileciteturn0file0L29-L33 I initially expected this to be our obvious repair, but current Week 3 analysis says otherwise: NBC has Carolina **DST #7 overall** this week. Seattle, KC and Minnesota are the top three, with Carolina firmly inside the second tier. citeturn416984view0turn416984view2\n\nSo I **would not dump Carolina just to make a move**. But I absolutely want us treating D/ST as a streaming position rather than marrying Carolina.\n\nThe defenses I want you to show me on your waiver wire are, roughly: **Seattle / KC / Minnesota if somehow available**, then Jacksonville, New England, Cincinnati, Cleveland, Houston, etc. Cincinnati is especially interesting because they opened the year with eight sacks across two games and were the No. 1 fantasy D/ST through two weeks; Cleveland also has a very attractive upcoming schedule after this week. citeturn930241news3\n\n### Kicker: Shrader is better than I expected\n\nYou have **Spencer Shrader vs Houston**, projected for 8.29 in the Yahoo export. fileciteturn0file0L23-L27 I would **not automatically replace him**.\n\nCurrent Week 3 kicker ranks have Shrader **#12 overall**, and he’s specifically being recommended as a streamer. He already hit from 58 this year and then made kicks from 42, 49 and 38 last week; he also gets Houston **indoors in Indianapolis**. citeturn416984view3turn416984view4\n\nThere are upgrades if they’re sitting there, though. The current top group includes **Aubrey, Tyler Loop, Eddy Piñeiro, Fairbairn, Butker, Jason Myers, McPherson and Cam Little** ahead of Shrader. citeturn416984view4\n\n### What I think of the team right now\n\n**Do not fuck with the foundation.** Cook + CeeDee is the kind of anchor combination that wins leagues, Davante/Ladd/Higgins gives you multiple WR combinations, and Andrews/Hockenson means we can eventually turn excess TE value into another position if the market gives us something stupid.\n\nRB2 is the spot I'm watching hardest. You’re starting **Jadarian Price**, while Lloyd, Monangai and Emanuel Wilson are your developmental/contingency RBs. fileciteturn0file0L9-L10 fileciteturn0file0L18-L20 If Price becomes a legitimate weekly RB2, the roster becomes **much harder to attack**.\n\nSo my priorities are:\n\n1. **Keep Carolina for this matchup unless a clearly better DST is free.**\n2. **Keep Shrader unless one of the premium kicker options is sitting there free.**\n3. **Spend almost no FAAB/waiver priority on K or DST.**\n4. **Use the waiver wire primarily to hunt breakout RB/WR upside**, because the starting lineup doesn't need another mediocre floor player.\n5. **Don't trade Higgins cheap because you're annoyed about where you drafted him.** His value to us now is independent of draft cost.\n\nSend me the **Yahoo available D/ST + kicker list** next. That’s where we can make this surgical — I’ll rank every available option against Carolina/Shrader and tell you exactly who I’d swap and who I’d leave alone."]}, "create_time": 1790284835.3737, "end_turn": true, "id": "4a06bf97-d6f8-459d-953c-8b4f8be2429c", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 320, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "5beaed8d-b42a-47c8-9fb4-856f61d64097", "cited_message_idx": 17, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_c7e7ff8f6f9c819182200fd1b637c140", "line_range": [8, 20], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 0, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_000000004e4481fda6a11450b355e19b", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "source": "my_files", "text": "| **QB**                                        | [Matthew Stafford](https://s.yimg.com/iu/apies/1.2/ikl7JSHSUNE_WRIe3s0BvQ--~C/YXBwaWQ9eXNwb3J0cztjaD0yMzM2O2NyPTE7Y3c9MTc5MjtkeD04NTY7ZHk9MDtmaT11bGNyb3A7aD0yMTU7cT0xMDA7dz0xNjU-/https://s.yimg.com/xe/i/us/sp/v/nfl_cutout/players_l/08192026/9265