te_time": 1790285144.672818, "end_turn": false, "id": "a902cc10-b8f4-450f-aba6-f6fc3bcd4c80", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": false, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 7, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "a5360386-ed60-4c57-b61a-e07cdd1106a3", "reasoning_end_time": 1790285144.6554554, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1790285136.971688, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "1d8ac1f0-d277-4ae0-afc2-31c4b020770c", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "126002e8-08a0-4216-ba9a-57996f703e37", "working_turn_id": "126002e8-08a0-4216-ba9a-57996f703e37"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790285144.672818, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yep — and I think you mean **Darren Waller**, not Walker. On *this* waiver wire, I’m with you: **Waller is much more interesting than Strange**.\n\nYour TE pool has Waller sitting there as a free agent, along with Barner, Ferguson, Dulcich, etc. fileciteturn2file0L1-L7 And Waller’s first two games have already given us something Strange hasn’t: **high-value red-zone involvement**. He scored twice last week on only three targets, and current Week 3 analysis still views him as a viable starter because Carolina is using him near the goal line. citeturn150294news1turn150294news6\n\nSo at TE, I’d actually shift the plan:\n\n**Hockenson stays our primary TE.**  \n**Waller > Strange as the second TE.**  \n**Andrews is the decision point.**\n\nThe reason I’m not immediately telling you to dump Andrews is that Andrews still has name/value and underlying usage. But if we’re serious about bench efficiency, carrying **Hockenson + Waller + Andrews** is still too many. I’d rather eventually turn one of Andrews/Waller into an RB stash or use Andrews as trade currency if anybody still values the name.\n\nOn your WR wire, though, there’s a bigger thing staring at us: **Xavier Worthy is just sitting there as a free agent at 62% rostered.** That is not a normal waiver-wire name. fileciteturn2file1L1-L1 He’d immediately jump near the top of my overall waiver priorities because he has an actual path to replacing Ladd in your flex, which is one of the problems we’re trying to solve.\n\nAfter Worthy, the WRs I care about from this list are **Makai Lemon, Wan'Dale Robinson, Rashod Bateman, Keenan Allen, Rashid Shaheed, Tre' Harris, Malik Washington**. Your pool confirms all of those names are available, with Lemon surprisingly still 51% rostered league-wide and Worthy 62%. fileciteturn2file1L3-L16\n\nSo now that I’ve seen **RB + TE + WR together**, my overall waiver board for *your roster* changes materially:\n\n1. **Xavier Worthy** — highest-impact add because he can attack the Ladd problem directly.\n2. **Emmett Johnson** — best RB stash for the roster construction we discussed.\n3. **Darren Waller** — definitely better use of the second-TE slot than Strange.\n4. **Braelon Allen** — pure contingent-upside RB stash.\n5. **Makai Lemon** — very interesting upside WR stash.\n6. **Singleton** — injury-away Tennessee swing.\n7. **Barner** — if Waller disappears, Barner is another legitimate TE streamer; current Week 3 waiver analysis specifically identifies both Waller and Barner as useful TE adds. citeturn150294news4\n\nAnd this is where I’d be careful: **don’t spend a roster move upgrading Strange to Waller before we secure Worthy if Worthy is truly free.** Wide receiver is the greater opportunity cost because Waller/Barner-type TEs are still sitting all over this pool, whereas a player with Worthy’s ceiling usually isn’t.\n\nSo my first two moves from everything you’ve shown me would be:\n\n**Drop Strange → add Xavier Worthy.**  \nThen find the next expendable slot for **Emmett Johnson**.\n\nAfter that, we decide whether the remaining TE pair should be **Hockenson/Andrews** or **Hockenson/Waller**. That’s the interesting decision now."]}, "create_time": 1790285144.675889, "end_turn": true, "id": "a7919982-ce8b-4a13-af81-15d850ea2eff", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 271, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "1992b9b2-4274-43ab-a07a-150e0947672c", "cited_message_idx": 88, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_f5c03e9409b881919b4e188bae890dbd", "line_range": [1, 7], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 2, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000a95881f5bc1ca6c6a60a4719", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "source": "my_files", "text": "| <br>[**Greg Dulcich**](https://s.yimg.com/iu/apies/1.2/s5eSp..qS8SALZcLml3MOQ--~C/YXBwaWQ9eXNwb3J0cztjaD0yMzM2O2NyPTE7Y3c9MTc5MjtkeD04NTY7ZHk9MDtmaT11bGNyb3A7aD0yMTU7cT0xMDA7dz0xNjU-/https://s.yimg.com/xe/i/us/sp/v/nfl_cutout/players_l/08192026/34036.2.png) | [**Greg Dulcich**](https://sports.yahoo.com/nfl/players/34036 \"Greg Dulcich\")[**Player Note**](https://sports.yahoo.com/nfl/players/34036/news)**Mia - TE**                                                                                                                                                                                    | [**Sun 1:00 pm vs **](https://sports.yahoo.com/nfl/kansas-city-chiefs-miami-dolphins-20260927015/)[**KC**](https://football.fantasysports.yahoo.com/f1/1327652/pointsagainst?pos=TE\\&n