g_start_time": 1790285272.8737993, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "48f5eb96-7c2b-4437-acad-cd3e100c933a", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "69255561-9136-440c-a724-e99d3de6a20d", "working_turn_id": "69255561-9136-440c-a724-e99d3de6a20d"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790285286.492557, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yeah — **now that I see the updated lineup, the first drop candidate is not Andrews. It’s MarShawn Lloyd.**\n\nYour bench is currently **Andrews, Higgins, Lloyd, Monangai, Emanuel Wilson, Waller**, with Pierce safely parked on IR. fileciteturn3file0L9-L15\n\nHere’s why Lloyd has moved to the front of the cut line: through two weeks he’s averaging only **10.5 touches and 31.5 yards**, played just 28% of the snaps last week, and Green Bay has turned into a three-man backfield with Chris Brooks and Kaleb Johnson. Lloyd also lost a fumble in Week 2 and didn’t get another touch afterward. Current analysis explicitly has him trending *away* from the lead role. citeturn428471news20turn428471news22\n\nMeanwhile, **Monangai is absolutely not a drop**. He’s averaging 12 touches and 91 total yards, has been extremely efficient, and currently sits RB17 in fantasy points per game despite a sub-40% snap share. He does have a knee issue we need to monitor, but the actual football usage says hold. citeturn428471news28turn428471news29\n\nAndrews also stays for now. His underlying numbers remain strong — **23.2% target share, 30% first-read share, 2.13 YPRR** — and he gets Dallas, which has been very favorable to TEs. citeturn428471news31 Waller is the upside TE experiment; Hockenson is the guy you’re riding.\n\nSo my current **drop ladder** is:\n\n1. **MarShawn Lloyd**\n2. **Emanuel Wilson**, depending on Seattle/Price usage\n3. **Darren Waller**, if the Carolina role proves touchdown-dependent\n4. **Mark Andrews**, only if his usage collapses rather than just his box score\n5. **Nobody else**\n\nLadd is nowhere near this conversation. He’s starting in your flex and still 98% rostered. fileciteturn3file0L8-L8 And Higgins definitely stays; he’s basically luxury depth right now. fileciteturn3file0L10-L10\n\nSo if **Emmett Johnson is still free**, I actually like **Lloyd → Emmett Johnson** more than Andrews → Emmett.\n\nThat lets us keep all three TE shots for one more week **without sacrificing the better RB stashes**."]}, "create_time": 1790285286.494833, "end_turn": true, "id": "49cd0409-9091-4e88-bafb-08785d8ea483", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 257, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "de846bfb-c86e-4998-9c30-82db887170fc", "cited_message_idx": 113, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_33738f3311a481919526c6623b5ffbcd", "line_range": [9, 15], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 3, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000085481fda77ec5b5dbc3e7b4", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "source": "my_files", "text": "| **BN**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | [Mark Andrews](https://s.yimg.com/iu/apies/1.2/C8Uz9DcdtJJwGQKsCrP7hw--~C/YXBwaWQ9eXNwb3J0cztjaD0yMzM2O2NyPTE7Y3c9MTc5MjtkeD04NTY7ZHk9MDtmaT11bGNyb3A7aD0yMTU7cT0xMDA7dz0xNjU-