_deny": [], "parent_id": "cc32ecea-7754-4ff3-8130-d39ace202684", "reasoning_end_time": 1790284946.1001341, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1790284940.2322698, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "3fe4c360-482e-4eb7-95b6-58d91baab733", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "61e7c709-84cf-4aee-8733-17017dfb7124", "working_turn_id": "61e7c709-84cf-4aee-8733-17017dfb7124"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790284946.332069, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yep — this is exactly the kind of RB waiver pool I wanted to see. And **I would not dump Emanuel Wilson for most of these guys**. He’s actually one of the hotter Week 3 waiver adds league-wide right now. citeturn732193search16turn732193search17\n\nFrom *your actual available list*, the names that matter are **Emmett Johnson, Braelon Allen, Kamara, Kaleb Johnson, and maybe Singleton as a pure upside lottery ticket**. Your export confirms all of them are sitting there as free agents. fileciteturn1file0L3-L11 fileciteturn1file0L21-L26\n\nMy order **for your roster specifically** would be:\n\n1. **Emmett Johnson** — this is my favorite stash on that screen. He was already identified in preseason as the KC RB2 to target, and he’s now a recommended Week 3 add in 10-team formats. That’s exactly your style: cheap bench player whose value can explode if the backfield changes. citeturn732193news10turn732193search17  \n2. **Braelon Allen** — another legit contingency/upside back, not just filler. He’s still being recommended in 12-team leagues. citeturn732193search17  \n3. **Alvin Kamara** — interesting name, but much more floor than lottery-ticket ceiling at this stage. Current waiver guidance actually has him below the explosive contingency backs. citeturn732193search17  \n4. **Kaleb Johnson** — deeper speculative add. The market is moving toward him, but he’s still more “stash and see” than immediate answer. citeturn732193search16turn732193search17  \n5. **Nicholas Singleton** — I still like the *idea* of the rookie, especially since we already talked about him, but right now the NFL opportunity isn’t showing up enough to make me sacrifice a stronger live stash. Yahoo has him only 2% rostered on this wire. fileciteturn1file0L22-L22\n\nThe important part: **Emanuel Wilson stays ahead of most of these.** Week 3 waiver tracking has him as the single biggest RB ownership riser in one dataset, and RotoBaller has him as an add in 10-team leagues. citeturn732193search16turn732193search17 So I retract the earlier thought that Wilson might be our easy cut.\n\nWhat I’d do right now is **hold Cook / Price / Wilson / Lloyd / Monangai**. The only RB waiver guy I’m seriously tempted to force onto this roster is **Emmett Johnson**. If we decide to add him, I’d rather create the slot by cutting **Brenton Strange** from that ridiculous third-TE pile than sacrificing one of these upside RBs.\n\nAnd there’s one important wrinkle: **Kaelon Black is not actually available yet** — Yahoo shows him on waivers until September 25 — and he’s ranked even higher than Emmett by some current waiver sources. fileciteturn1file0L9-L9 citeturn732193search17 So I’d keep an eye on him too.\n\n**Current Don RB bench philosophy:** don’t collect boring RB4s. Keep backs who can become an RB2 overnight.\n\nNext, send me the **WR waiver list**. That’s where I think we may find the more important move, because we need somebody who can start pressuring Ladd’s flex slot."]}, "create_time": 1790284946.397449, "end_turn": true, "id": "68e92349-c2d1-4529-b63d-46ee8882efa6", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 517, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "fil