ation_sec": 3, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "5d2fefb1-6f24-47e6-917f-b017183d2cce", "reasoning_end_time": 1790284999.2789488, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1790284995.3231974, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "64f7e2fe-e3ac-4ea5-a2ba-186b4e076c11", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "8a1712c7-7fea-4b7b-a8b8-93e2d87f3c29", "working_turn_id": "8a1712c7-7fea-4b7b-a8b8-93e2d87f3c29"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790284999.291932, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["**I think you’re right: one of the three TEs needs to become another RB lottery ticket.** And between Andrews and Strange, **I’d cut Strange first and keep Andrews.**\n\nThe reason is usage, not name value. Through two games, Andrews has a **23.2% target share, 30% first-read share, 67.6% route share, and 2.13 yards per route run**. That’s still strong underlying TE usage despite the mediocre fantasy output so far. citeturn829033news3turn829033news8 Strange, meanwhile, is sitting at just a **9.6% target share and 10.5% first-read share**, and current Week 3 analysis has him only TE23 in points per game. citeturn829033news9\n\nSo your TE room should become:\n\n**Hockenson — ride him for now.**  \n**Andrews — hold as the second bullet / rebound asset.**  \n**Strange — expendable.**\n\nThen I’d turn Strange into **Braelon Allen or Emmett Johnson**. Both are available in your league; Allen is only 17% rostered and Emmett 32%. fileciteturn1file0L6-L7\n\nAnd knowing how you like to construct these benches, I actually like **Allen** a lot for you. You’re not looking for somebody who gives you 5.8 points when Price has a bad week. You want somebody sitting there who can suddenly become **a serious starting RB if the depth chart breaks his way**.\n\nSo I’d make the move:\n\n**DROP Brenton Strange → ADD Braelon Allen.**\n\nThen your RB stable becomes **Cook / Price / Lloyd / Monangai / Emanuel Wilson / Braelon Allen**, with Pierce occupying IR. That is a much better use of the roster slot than carrying three TEs. Your current roster confirms Strange is just sitting behind Hockenson and Andrews anyway. fileciteturn0file0L13-L20\n\nI would **not cut Andrews yet**. His box scores are annoying, but the underlying workload says there’s still something there. Strange is the redundant piece."]}, "create_time": 1790284999.294483, "end_turn": true, "id": "f38dc5fb-ce69-4332-87dd-653ebd5726da", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 960, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "5c012630-f2bf-47f3-aa0f-0b35ffc001cf", "cited_message_idx": 45, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_dc16cbae8b608191b24d0b34dc7b1de0", "line_range": [6, 7], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 1, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000065081fd904400604b1171c1", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "source": "my_files", "text": "| [****](https://football.fantasysports.yahoo.com/f1/1327652/addplayer?apid=40981 \"Add Player\") | [****](https://football.fantasysports.yahoo.com/f1/1327652/addplayerwatch?mid=12\\&apid=40981\\&crumb=playerwatch\\|KpTlnfGvIr1\\&done=https%3A%2F%2Ffootball.fantasysports.yahoo.com%2Ff1%2F1327652%2Fplayers%3Fpos%3Drb%26sort%3Dpts%26sdir%3D1%26status%3Da%26eteam%3Dall%26fteam%3Dnone%26stat1%3Ds_pw_3%2