-4cd5-8cd0-ddd07f66963f"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790285087.077694, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yep — **that’s exactly why Singleton is tempting but still third for me.**\n\nTennessee’s situation is legitimately interesting right now: **both Tony Pollard and Tyjae Spears missed Wednesday practice with ankle issues**, and Singleton is the next man up. He finally got four carries in Week 2, so there is a real injury-driven path to touches. citeturn437382news0turn437382news1turn437382news3\n\nBut your committee concern is the key distinction. If Pollard and Spears are active, Singleton can disappear. And even if one misses time, Tennessee’s run blocking has been poor, so you’re betting on both **opportunity opening up and the offense supporting it**. citeturn437382news1\n\nThat’s why I’d rank the stashes for **this roster**:\n\n1. **Emmett Johnson** — best combination of *role already growing + contingency upside*. Andy Reid has explicitly said Johnson will get more snaps to lighten Kenneth Walker’s workload, and Johnson has produced 103 scrimmage yards on only 14 touches. citeturn437382news19turn437382news10\n2. **Braelon Allen** — cleaner classic lottery ticket. His independent role isn’t huge, but if the backfield opens, he has the body/TD profile to become useful fast. He already scored in Week 2. citeturn437382news21\n3. **Nicholas Singleton** — arguably the most explosive speculative bet, but the current path is messier because Pollard + Spears are both ahead of him when healthy.\n\nAnd Singleton is just **2% rostered** in your Yahoo league, so we probably don’t need to panic-grab him this second. fileciteturn1file0L22-L22\n\nSo I still like:\n\n**Strange → Emmett Johnson.**\n\nThen we watch Singleton very closely through the rest of this week. If Pollard and/or Spears trend toward being out, **Singleton immediately moves way up the board**. If both are cleared, I’d rather let somebody else occupy the Tennessee committee headache.\n\nYour instinct is right: **in a shallow/redraft bench, chase pathways to 15+ touches, not permanent 7-touch committee roles.**"]}, "create_time": 1790285087.080311, "end_turn": true, "id": "47a65558-4700-49ab-8c92-4275ae2a26f0", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 1564, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "5c012630-f2bf-47f3-aa0f-0b35ffc001cf", "cited_message_idx": 45, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_dc16cbae8b608191b24d0b34dc7b1de0", "line_range": [22, 22], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 1, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000065081fd904400604b1171c1", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "source": "my_files", "text": "| [****](https://football.fantasysports.yahoo.com/f1/1327652/addplayer?apid=42763 \"Add Player\") | [****](https://football.fantasysports.yahoo.com/f1/1327652/addplayerwatch?mid=12\\&apid=42763\\&crumb=playerwatch\\|KpTlnfGvIr1\\&done=https%3A%2F%2Ffootball.fantasysports.yahoo.com%2Ff1%2F1327652%2Fplayers%3Fpos%3Drb%26sort%3Dpts%26sdir%3D1%26status%3Da%26eteam%3Dall%26fteam%3Dnone%26stat1%3Ds_pw_3%26jsenabled%3D1 \"Add to Watch List\") | [**Nicholas Singleton**](https://s.yimg.com/iu/apies/1.2/ytgj.Qp7pnQP6BEOBI30cA--~C/YXBwaWQ9eXNwb3J0cztjaD0yMzM2O2NyPTE7Y3c9MTc5MjtkeD04NTY7ZHk9MDtmaT11bGNyb3A7aD0yMTU7cT0xMDA7dz0xNjU-/https://s.yimg.com/xe/i/us/sp/v/nfl_cutout/players_l/08262026/42763.1.png) | [**Nicholas Singleton**](https://sports.yahoo.com/nfl/player