itor, but the actual football usage says hold. citeturn428471news28turn428471news29\n\nAndrews also stays for now. His underlying numbers remain strong — **23.2% target share, 30% first-read share, 2.13 YPRR** — and he gets Dallas, which has been very favorable to TEs. citeturn428471news31 Waller is the upside TE experiment; Hockenson is the guy you’re riding.\n\nSo my current **drop ladder** is:\n\n1. **MarShawn Lloyd**\n2. **Emanuel Wilson**, depending on Seattle/Price usage\n3. **Darren Waller**, if the Carolina role proves touchdown-dependent\n4. **Mark Andrews**, only if his usage collapses rather than just his box score\n5. **Nobody else**\n\nLadd is nowhere near this conversation. He’s starting in your flex and still 98% rostered. fileciteturn3file0L8-L8 And Higgins definitely stays; he’s basically luxury depth right now. fileciteturn3file0L10-L10\n\nSo if **Emmett Johnson is still free**, I actually like **Lloyd → Emmett Johnson** more than Andrews → Emmett.\n\nThat lets us keep all three TE shots for one more week **without sacrificing the better RB stashes**."]}, "create_time": 1790285286.494833, "end_turn": true, "id": "49cd0409-9091-4e88-bafb-08785d8ea483", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 257, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "de846bfb-c86e-4998-9c30-82db887170fc", "cited_message_idx": 113, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_33738f3311a481919526c6623b5ffbcd", "line_range": [9, 15], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 3, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000085481fda77ec5b5dbc3e7b4", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "so